<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Adversarial examples</h3>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present two adversarial examples, one from each level of the adversary: a systemic sample, which exposes a gap in how the composition program combines predicates, and a local sample, which exposes a single predicate misjudging an input within its own scope. Both examples target intermediate decompositions produced during the search.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Systemic adversarial examples</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="2538.1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 2538.1" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,2538.1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#595959;" fill="#595959" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.77 L 0 2535.34 C 0 2536.86 1.24 2538.1 2.77 2538.1 L 474.61 2538.1 C 476.14 2538.1 477.38 2536.86 477.38 2535.34 L 477.38 2.77 C 477.38 1.24 476.14 0 474.61 0 L 2.77 0 C 1.24 0 0 1.24 0 2.77 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FAFAFA;" fill="#FAFAFA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 2.77 L 0.69 2520.2 L 476.68 2520.2 L 476.68 2.77 C 476.68 1.62 475.76 0.69 474.61 0.69 L 2.77 0.69 C 1.62 0.69 0.69 1.62 0.69 2.77 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#595959;" fill="#595959" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 2520.89 L 0.69 2535.34 C 0.69 2536.48 1.62 2537.41 2.77 2537.41 L 474.61 2537.41 C 475.76 2537.41 476.68 2536.48 476.68 2535.34 L 476.68 2520.89 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.55 2524.83)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="426.6"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.83em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Task definition</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.55 12.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.49em;--ltx-fo-height:180.54em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="2500.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 2498.17)" width="491.08"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.49em;">
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A fitness and wellness recommendation system generates short coaching
messages that nudge users toward healthier habits. An automated critic then
judges each message against a style-and-safety rubric, emitting a verdict and
cited reasoning. Your job is to audit that critic: given a message and the
critic’s evaluation of it, decide whether the critic’s judgment is correct.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your task is to classify a given sample into exactly one of three labels:
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Pass’</span>, <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Fail’</span>, or <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Bug’</span>. A <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’sample’</span> consists
of a fitness-coaching message together with the underlying evaluator’s verdict
and cited reasoning (e.g., word count, fired rule). You must always select the
best-fitting label.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Seven Rubric Dimensions (for reference):</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">word_count: under 18 words</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">sentence_count: a single sentence</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">actionable: recommends a concrete and relevant exercise related action the user can carry out</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">non_judgmental: don’t use judgmental language</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">no_gamification: avoid messages that include gamification</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">safety_first: does not require the user to do actions that are unsafe for their body or current state (e.g., push through sharp pain)</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">system_grounded: if the </span><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">system_state</span><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> field is non-empty then the </span><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">coaching_message</span><span id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> must address the advice category or the user’s weakest dimension - any unrelated topic violates this.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Label Definitions &amp; Boundaries:</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pass:<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Positive Definition: The underlying coaching message adheres to ALL seven rubric dimensions AND the evaluator correctly accepted it.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Boundary Rules: Only label <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Pass’</span> when both the message is clean and the evaluator agrees.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fail:<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Positive Definition: The coaching message violates at least one of
the seven rubric dimensions AND the evaluator correctly rejected it, citing an applicable reason. Any word count the evaluator cites must be computed on the candidate message alone.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Boundary Rules: Only label <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Fail’</span> when the violation is real and the evaluator’s cited reason matches it.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Bug:<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Positive Definition: The evaluator’s output is wrong in any of the
following ways:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">False positive: a clean message was rejected.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">False negative: a violating message was accepted.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Right verdict, wrong reason: the message truly violates some
dimension, but the reason cited by the evaluator does not apply.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Inconsistent verdict/reasoning: if </span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_verdict</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is
</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Fail’</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> then </span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_reasoning</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> must cite at least one
reason; a </span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Pass’</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that nonetheless cites a violation is a
</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Bug’</span><span id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Boundary Rules: Any of the above sub-cases makes the sample a
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">’Bug’</span>. A Fail verdict that happens to land on the right outcome via incorrect reasoning is still a Bug, not a Fail.</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sample Layout:</span></span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each sample is a series of XML-tagged blocks of the form <span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;field_name&gt;value&lt;/field_name&gt;</span>, one per field. Fields may be omitted when not present.</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">system_state</span><span id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: optional user profile / state / advice
category / intensity metadata (already separated from the coaching message).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">coaching_message</span><span id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: the candidate message text only (this is
what the rubric dimensions are checked against).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_verdict</span><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: </span><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Pass’</span><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> or </span><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Fail’</span><span id="A5.I3.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A5.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_reasoning</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: a JSON array listing each violated dimension
the evaluator flagged, e.g.
</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">["Dimension": "non_judgmental", "Evidence": "you always", ...]</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Each entry has a Dimension (one of the seven rubric dimensions) and
Evidence — either a specific snippet from the </span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">coaching_message</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
or a short free-text explanation of why that dimension is violated. Its
value is empty when </span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_verdict</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Pass’</span><span id="A5.I3.i4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Decision Procedure:</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Check the </span><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">coaching_message</span><span id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> against each of the seven
rubric dimensions to determine whether it should Pass or Fail.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Compare the </span><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_verdict</span><span id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to step 1’s conclusion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If verdicts disagree, the label is </span><span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Bug’</span><span id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (false positive or
false negative).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If verdicts agree and the verdict is Pass, the label is
</span><span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Pass’</span><span id="A5.I4.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If verdicts agree and the verdict is Fail, verify that every entry in
</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">eval_reasoning</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> names a Dimension that is genuinely violated by
the </span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">coaching_message</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> AND its Evidence is consistent with that
violation. If that check fails, the label is </span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Bug’</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; otherwise
</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’Fail’</span><span id="A5.I4.i5.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A5.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<span id="A5.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output only the chosen label.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Examples:</span></span>
